  AUTHORS   Zhou,Y. and Shen,S.
  TITLE     MiR-520f acts as a biomarker for the diagnosis of lung cancer
  JOURNAL   Medicine (Baltimore) 98 (30), e16546 (2019)
   PUBMED   31348274
  REMARK    GeneRIF: Serum miR-520f was down-regulated in lung cancer patients
            compared with healthy group. Moreover, the expression of miR-520f
            was significantly associated with advanced TNM stage and
            metastasis. The area under the curve (AUC) value of ROC curve was
            0.888, suggesting that miR-520f could be a diagnostic biomarker for
            lung cancer. The cut-off value of serum miR-520f for lung cancer
            diagnosis was 1.815.
