REFERENCE   2  (bases 1 to 99)
  AUTHORS   Jiao Y, Yang H, Qian J, Gong Y, Liu H, Wu S, Cao L and Tang L.
  TITLE     miR36645P suppresses the proliferation and metastasis of gastric
            cancer by attenuating the NFkappaB signaling pathway through
            targeting MTDH
  JOURNAL   Int J Oncol 54 (3), 845-858 (2019)
   PUBMED   30628643
  REMARK    GeneRIF: miR36645P is downregulated in gastric cancer (GC) tissues
            and is positively associated with the prognosis of patients with
            GC. miR36645P knockdown promots the proliferation and metastasis of
            GC cells in vitro and in vivo. miR36645P reduces metadherin (MTDH)
            expression and downregulates the nuclear factor (NF)kappaB
            signaling pathway. miR36645P has potential to be an independent
            prognostic factor and biomarker in GC.
