  AUTHORS   Zhu Y, Xie J and Sun H.
  TITLE     Three miRNAs cooperate with host genes involved in human
            cardiovascular disease
  JOURNAL   Hum. Genomics 13 (1), 40 (2019)
   PUBMED   31464655
  REMARK    GeneRIF: We found that the three protein-coding genes functionally
            interact with targets of their intronic miRNAs, i.e., miR-3182,
            miR-6863, and miR-5582, in a tissue-specific pattern.
            Publication Status: Online-Only
REFERENCE   2  (bases 1 to 68)
  AUTHORS   Zheng A, Song X, Zhang L, Zhao L, Mao X, Wei M and Jin F.
  TITLE     Long non-coding RNA LUCAT1/miR-5582-3p/TCF7L2 axis regulates breast
            cancer stemness via Wnt/beta-catenin pathway
  JOURNAL   J. Exp. Clin. Cancer Res. 38 (1), 305 (2019)
   PUBMED   31300015
  REMARK    GeneRIF: LUCAT1 might be a significant biomarker to evaluate
            prognosis in breast cancer survivors. LUCAT1 increased BCCs
            stem-like properties and BCSCs stemness by competitively binding
            miR-5582-3p with TCF7L2 and enhancing the Wnt/beta-catenin
            signaling pathway.
            Publication Status: Online-Only
REFERENCE   3  (bases 1 to 68)
  AUTHORS   Abedini Bakhshmand E, Mohammad Soltani B, Fasihi A and Mowla SJ.
  TITLE     Hsa-miR-5582-3P regulatory effect on TGFbeta signaling through
            targeting of TGFbeta-R1, TGFbeta-R2, SMAD3, and SMAD4 transcripts
  JOURNAL   J. Cell. Biochem. 119 (12), 9921-9930 (2018)
   PUBMED   30129155
  REMARK    GeneRIF: miR-5582-3P reduces the TGFbeta/SMAD signaling pathway
            through downregulation of TGFbeta-R1, TGFbeta-R2, SMAD3, and SMAD4
            transcripts. These data introduce miR-5582-3P as a potential tumor
            suppressors-miR.
REFERENCE   4  (bases 1 to 68)
  AUTHORS   An HJ, Kwak SY, Yoo JO, Kim JS, Bae IH, Park MJ, Cho MY, Kim J and
            Han YH.
  TITLE     Novel miR-5582-5p functions as a tumor suppressor by inducing
            apoptosis and cell cycle arrest in cancer cells through direct
            targeting of GAB1, SHC1, and CDK2
  JOURNAL   Biochim. Biophys. Acta 1862 (10), 1926-1937 (2016)
   PUBMED   27475256
  REMARK    GeneRIF: miR-5582-5p induced apoptosis and cell cycle arrest in
            cancer cells, but not in normal cells. GAB1, SHC1, and CDK2 were
            identified as direct targets of miR-5582-5p.
